    "title": "Explore Tree Rings and Nature Journaling at Mason Regional Park Event for Irvine Residents - NewsBreak",
    "text": "54 minutes ago OC Park Naturalists are hosting an event at Mason Regional Park in Irvine for participants aged 12 and older. The event includes nature journaling, a guided walk, and an introduction to dendrology, which is the study of tree rings. Activities will take place at 18712 University Drive.\nParticipants must register in advance and sign a waiver. Those under 18 must be accompanied by a parent or guardian. The event is rated as easy, with a difficulty level of 1 out of 5. Attendees should bring water, wear closed-toed shoes, and use sun protection. Parking costs $5 per car. Carpooling is suggested because parking is limited. The event may be canceled if there is bad weather.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
